  bootwright / cluster rsh
      Open an SSH session on a cluster node's Machine as the Machine's resolved identity;
      confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit status. The session
      runs as the identity the Machine's desired state authorizes, over a host key proved
      before any credential is offered; an unproved key is confirmed interactively or refused.
      The exit status is the client's. The session opens on the Machine behind one node of a
      managed CephCluster: --node selects the node by name, then by FQDN, and defaults to the
      first node in name order. External CephClusters are inapplicable, and sessions on
      OpenShiftClusters are not yet available.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster rsh [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select the exact object name (required)
      --node  Select a declared node by name, then FQDN (default: the first node in name order)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright cluster rsh --context lab --name storage --node node-1
